        <ezobject:attribute xmlns:ezremote="http://ez.no/ezobject" ezremote:id="276" ezremote:identifier="body" name="Body" type="ezxmltext">
          <section xmlns:image="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/image/" xmlns:xhtml="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/xhtml/" xmlns:custom="http://ez.no/namespaces/ezpublish3/custom/">
            <section>
              <section>
                <header>Inside Exponential</header>
                <paragraph>This guide is premium content: it is in the "Premium content" section, which only subscribers may read. It shows how sections and roles limit who sees what.</paragraph>
              </section>
              <section>
                <header>The request</header>
                <paragraph>A request is matched to a siteaccess, the URL alias is resolved to a node, permissions are checked and the view is rendered from cached templates. Velocity keeps the compiled code in memory between requests.</paragraph>
              </section>
              <section>
                <header>The storage</header>
                <paragraph>Content lives in versioned objects with translated attributes. Files are stored in a cluster-aware file handler, so several web servers can share one storage.</paragraph>
              </section>
              <section>
                <header>Scaling out</header>
                <paragraph>Add web servers behind a load balancer, move files to the cluster handler, put Solr or Elasticsearch next to the database for search, and let the response cache absorb the peaks.</paragraph>
              </section>
            </section>
          </section>
